      "definition": "(J) A state agency shall notify an employee recalled from layoff of the offer of reinstatement or reemployment either by certified letter or, if the agency has record of an internet identifier of record associated with the employee, by ordinary mail and by that internet identifier of record. As used in this division, \"internet identifier of record\" has the same meaning as in section 9.312 of the Revised Code.",
